# Generated by tools/spheres_catalog_lst.py; OGC: catalog-OGL.txt
# https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving
Veilweaving Sphere	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBaseSphere.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Spheres Casting Core	DEFINE:SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DEFINE:SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_SPHERESHAPERSTALENT_COUNT|0	DEFINE:SPHERES_CL_VEILWEAVING|SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL	DEFINE:SPHERES_DC_VEILWEAVING|10+floor(SPHERES_CL_VEILWEAVING/2)+SPHERES_CASTING_ABILITY	DESC:Veilweaving Sphere: You can tap into the powers of the akashic library, using your magic to bind veils of magical construction to your body and to infuse them with your power. Further deepening your devotion to this sphere of magic can allow you to better manipulate the veils you shape, utilize essence to empower your other abilities, and even use your essence to disrupt your foes. Veilweaving: You count your combined levels in your casting classes and any veilweaving classes as your veilweaving level and your casting ability modifier as your veilweaving modifier for the purposes of the veils you shape, abilities that determine their effects based on your veilweaving level, and for acquiring and utilizing akashic feats. You also count as having levels in a veilweaving class when you take this sphere for the purposes of abilities and feats that require you to have levels in such a class. If a single class is both a veilweaver and a casting class at the same time it only counts as a single level in a veilweaving class for these purposes. Known Veils: When you gain this sphere, you immediately learn a veil of your choice. This veil must be able to be shaped in one of the following chakra slots: Belt, Body, Chest, Feet, Hands, Head, Headband, Neck, Shoulders, or Wrists. Shape Veil: When you rest to recover your spell points for the day, you can choose to shape a single veil you know. This follows the normal rules for shaping veils [you can only shape a single veil in any slot]. If you are able to bind that veil to the chakra you shaped it to, you may bind that veil as part of this process. You can shape veils to the following chakra slots: Belt, Body, Chest, Feet, Hands, Head, Headband, Neck, Shoulders, or Wrists. Shaping veils, and the veils you shape using this sphere do not count as sphere effects for any purposes. If you take this sphere on a character who can shape veils from a non-sphere source [such as a base-class veilweaver like vizier], this ability does not increase the maximum number of veils you may shape each day. This restriction does not apply if you only have the ability to shape a specific veil from a racial trait or class feature, or a subset of veils from a class feature, such as the sphere daevic’s passions class feature or the stormbound’s stormweaving ability. Condense and Draw Essence: As a swift action, you can spend any number of spell points to gain half that many points of temporary essence [rounded down, minimum 0]. You may only ever have a total amount of temporary essence using this ability at any time equal to your caster level with this sphere. These points of temporary essence persist until you rest to recover your spell points. Additionally, as a swift action, you can choose to burn any number of points of temporary essence granted by this ability to gain a number of temporary spell points equal to the amount of temporary essence burned. These temporary spell points last for 1 minute. Essence Capacity: Your veils and essence receptacles gained through this sphere have a maximum amount of essence that can be invested into them, based on your character level. This maximum may be increased by talents, feats, or magic items. / Character Level / Essence Capacity / 0 - 5 / 1 / 6 - 11 / 2 / 12 - 17 / 3 / 18 - 20 / 4 Essence: For each [essence] talent you take, you gain a single point of essence in addition to the normal effects of the talent. Most [essence] talents allow you to invest essence in them for a greater effect, in those cases, an [essence] talent has the same essence capacity as a veil you could shape using this sphere. Associated Veilweaving Feats: Some talents presented in this sphere overlap the function of existing feats. Such a feat is listed in the talent as an associated feat. Talents with associated feats allow a character to qualify for feats that have the associated feat as a prerequisite, including any prerequisites the associated feat normally requires. Unless noted, talents do not stack with their associated feats. If you have the Veilweaving sphere and would gain an associated veilweaving feat, you may instead choose to gain the talent it is associated with. You must still meet the prerequisites for a talent gained this way. Basic Talents with Prerequisites: Some basic talents of the Veilweaving sphere possess prerequisites that must be met before they can be selected. These talents are not advanced talents, despite only advanced talents normally having prerequisites. A caster cannot use temporary increases to caster level, such as those provided by an implement, to qualify for basic talents with a caster level prerequisite. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving
Veilweaving - Capacity Increase	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,3	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 3rd The maximum amount of essence that can be invested in your essence receptacles increases by 1. You may take this talent an additional time at 9th caster level, and 15th caster level; the effects stack. This talent does not stack with the improved essence capacity class feature or any other ability that grants an increase to the capacity of all of your essence receptacles. When determining your capacity, compare the total capacity increase granted by this talent to the total capacity increase granted by your other abilities and take the higher value. This talent does stack with any ability that grants a capacity increase to a single veil, or a subset of your normal veils [such as the daevic’s improved passion capacity class feature]. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc13
Veilweaving - Enhanced Capacity	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you rest to recover your spell points for the day, choose one essence receptacle such as a veil, a talent that can be invested, a magic item designed to contain essence, or a class feature. Your essence capacity for that receptacle is increased by 1. Each time you rest to recover spell points, you can change the receptacle that benefits from this talent. You may take this talent an additional time at 7th caster level and every 6 caster levels thereafter. Each time you take this talent, you can apply its effects to one additional receptacle while shaping your veils. You can’t apply this talent’s effects more than once to the same receptacle. Associated feat: Enhanced Capacity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc14
Veilweaving - Shared Veil	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you shape your veils for the day you can choose to shape a single one of your veils onto an ally in Close range of you, instead of on yourself. You can change which ally this veil is shaped to as a standard action as long the new target is within Close range of you. If the ally leaves an area within Close range of you, it loses the benefits of the veil shaped to it until it returns within range of you. The ally gains the benefits of any essence you have invested in the shared veil. The ally must have the chakra slot for this shared veil available, or else it cannot be shared with that ally. You cannot bind a veil shared with an ally with this talent, even if you or the ally could normally bind veils of the shared veils chakra slot. This talent can be selected additional times, allowing you to share an additional veil each day for each selection after the first. Associated feat: Shared Veil. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc15
Veilweaving - Shift Veil	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:By spending 1 spell point as a move action that provokes attacks of opportunity, you can unshape one of your existing veils and instantly reshape the released energy into a new veil you know. The veil you shape using this ability cannot be bound to a chakra until you have spent one hour in meditation, even if the veil you unshaped was already bound. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc16
Veilweaving - Sphereshaper’s Talent	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_SPHERESHAPERSTALENT_COUNT|1	DESC:When you shape your veils for the day, choose a single veil you shaped that grants you a sphere. You gain a talent of your choice associated with that sphere that you meet the prerequisites for. This talent counts as a talent granted by that veil for all purposes. If that veil is unshaped, you lose this talent until you rest and reshape your veils for the day. If you used the Shift Veil talent [or a similar ability] to unshape that veil, if the new veil also grants a sphere you may gain a talent from that sphere. You may take this talent multiple times, allowing you to gain a talent for each time it is selected. You may select the same veil multiple times or may select a different veil for each time you have selected this talent. Associated feat: Sphereshaper’s Talent. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc17
Veilweaving - Veil Knowledge	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You learn one additional veil of your choice. If you do not have a [tradition] talent, you learn an additional veil plus one additional veil per 5 caster levels. These veils must be able to be shaped in one of the following chakra slots: Belt, Body, Chest, Feet, Hands, Head, Headband, Neck, Shoulders, or Wrists. You make take this talent additional times, learning an additional veil each time you select it. If you take a [tradition] talent, select one veil learned from this talent for each time you have selected it. You lose knowledge of the veils you did not select if they are not part of your [tradition]. Associated feat: Shape Veil. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc18
Veilweaving - Shape Additional Veil	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,3	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 3rd When you rest to recover spell points for the day, you may shape an additional veil you know. If you do not have a [tradition] talent, you learn an additional veil of your choice as well. You may take this talent an additional time at 6th caster level and every 3 caster levels thereafter; the effects stack. If you have the ability to shape veils from a non-sphere source, this talent cannot be taken if it would allow you to shape more veils than 1 + 1 per 3 Hit Dice you possess. This restriction does not apply if you only have the ability to shape a specific veil from a racial trait or class feature, or a subset of veils from a class feature, such as the sphere daevic’s passions class feature or the stormbound’s stormweaving ability. If you take a [tradition] talent, you lose knowledge of the veils you selected with this talent if they are not part of your [tradition]. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc19
Veilweaving - Bind Feet Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,2	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 2nd You can now bind veils to the Feet slot. Associated feat: Access Low Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc21
