Veilweaving - Bind Head Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,6	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 6th You can now bind veils to the Head slot. Associated feat: Access Low Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc23
Veilweaving - Bind Wrists Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,8	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 8th You can now bind veils to the Wrists slot. Associated feat: Access Middle Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc24
Veilweaving - Bind Shoulders Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,10	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 10th You can now bind veils to the Shoulders slot. Associated feat: Access Middle Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc25
Veilweaving - Bind Headband Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,12	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 12th You can now bind veils to the Headband slot. Associated feat: Access Middle Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc26
Veilweaving - Bind Belt Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,14	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 14th You can now bind veils to the Belt slot. Associated feat: Access High Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc27
Veilweaving - Bind Neck Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,14	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 14th You can now bind veils to the Neck slot. Associated feat: Access High Chakra Slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc28
Veilweaving - Bind Chest Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,18	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 18th You can now bind veils to the Chest chakra slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc29
Veilweaving - Bind Body Chakra	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CASTER_LEVEL,20	DESC:Prerequisites: Caster level 20th You can now bind veils to the Body chakra slot. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc30
Veilweaving - Chakra Disruption	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest essence in this talent. By spending 1 spell point as a standard action, you can attempt to disrupt one of the targets chakra slots. Select one of the targets chakra slots [Hands, Head, Feet, Headband, Shoulders, Wrists, Belt, Neck, Body, or Chest] and make a melee touch attack against the target. If you hit, you disrupt the selected chakra slot. Veils shaped in that slot have the saving throws of their abilities reduced by 2 [including the saving throws of any spheres or talents granted by that veil], their maximum essence capacity reduced by 2 [to a minimum of 0], and the target suffers a -2 penalty to attack rolls and CMB when using the abilities of veils shaped in that chakra slot [or the abilities of any spheres granted by that veil, or any weapons created by that veil]. These penalties last for 1 round, plus an additional round for each essence invested in this talent. Using this ability multiple times on the same chakra slot resets this ability duration, and worsens the penalties applied by this talent by 1. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc32
Veilweaving - Draining Touch	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest essence in this talent. As a standard action, you can make a melee touch attack that drains the essence of a creature. This ability does not provoke attacks of opportunity. If your attack hits, the target takes 1d8 points of untyped damage, plus an additional 1d8 per point of essence invested in this talent, and you gain 1 temporary essence for 1 minute. If the targeted creature has an essence pool of at least 1, you gain an additional point of temporary essence and inflict 1 point of essence burn on the target. You may only have a maximum number of temporary essence from this talent equal to your casting ability modifier. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc33
Veilweaving - Emergency Investment	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:By spending a spell point as an immediate action, you can choose to either reinvest your essence between your veils and other essence receptacles, or you may use your condense and draw essence ability. If you gain temporary essence as part of using that ability, you may immediately invest it in an essence receptacle. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc34
Veilweaving - Entwined Allocation	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you spend a swift action to use an ability, you may reallocate your essence as part of using that ability. You may still only reallocate your essence as part of using a swift action once per round, even if you can use multiple swift actions each round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc35
Veilweaving - Essence Disruption	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest essence in this talent. You may spend 1 spell point as a standard action to attempt to disrupt the flow of essence within the target. Make a melee touch attack against the target. If you hit, the target cannot invest or reinvest essence to or from their essence receptacles for 1 round, plus 1 round per point of essence invested in this talent [minimum 1 round]. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc36
Veilweaving - Essence Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:As a standard action, you may make a single weapon attack in combination with an [essence] talent that targets a single creature. This casting cannot be reduced below a standard action and does not provoke attacks of opportunity, unless as usual if making a ranged attack. If the target is struck by the attack, it is also affected by the [essence] talent. If using a scatter weapon, the [essence] talent only applies to a single target, chosen at the time of the attack. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc37
Veilweaving - Essence-Infused Magic	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you select this talent, choose one magic sphere you possess [except the Veilweaving sphere], and one of the following options: Range, MSB/MSD, or Damage. You cannot use this talent to enhance spheres you only have access to through a veil. You can invest essence in this talent to improve the effects of the chosen magic sphere, based on your chosen option. Range: You gain a +2 insight bonus per essence invested in this talent to your caster level for the purposes of determining the range of the abilities of the chosen sphere. MSB / MSD: You gain a +1 insight bonus to your MSB and MSD with the chosen sphere per point of essence invested in this talent. Damage: You gain a +2 insight bonus to damage rolls of the abilities of the chosen sphere per point of essence invested in this talent. The damage is of the same type as the cast ability’s damage. If the ability deals multiple types of damage, choose a single damage type for this bonus damage. This talent can be selected multiple times, allowing you to select a different sphere and option each time you select it. Each selection of this talent counts as a separate essence receptacle. You may choose the same sphere multiple times with additional selections of this talent, choosing an additional option for that sphere each time it is selected. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc38
Veilweaving - Essence-Infused Resistance	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest essence in this talent. When you invest essence in this talent, choose a saving throw type [Fortitude, Reflex, or Will] you gain an insight bonus to saving throws of that type equal to the amount of essence invested in this talent. Associated Feats: Chakra-Enhanced Fortitude, Weaver’s Reflexes, Will of the Daeva Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc39
Veilweaving - Extra Essence	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You gain 1 point of essence. This point is in addition to the normal 1 point of essence granted by taking this [essence] talent. Associated Feat: Extra Essence. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc40
Veilweaving - Mage’s Binding	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest non-temporary essence in this talent. Whenever an ability or sphere effect would require an expenditure of spell points, you may bind points of essence invested in this talent to reduce the spell point cost of that ability as you use it. For each essence bound, reduce the spell point cost of the ability by 1 [to a minimum of 0]. This reduction only applies to that use of the ability, not towards any other times you use the ability. Essence bound to this talent cannot be burned. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc41
Veilweaving - Suppressing Touch	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You can invest essence in this talent. By spending 1 spell point as a standard action, you can make a melee touch attack to attempt to suppress a shaped veil or essence receptacle of the attacked creature. This ability does not provoke attacks of opportunity. If your attack hits, the target must make a Will save or have one of its currently invested essence receptacles of your choice suppressed for 1 round, plus 1 round per point of essence invested in this talent. While the receptacle is suppressed its user does not gain any of the passive benefits of the ability, nor can they use any active abilities granted by it. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc42
Veilweaving - Veilwarding	CATEGORY:Spheres Magic Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Veilweaving	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Veilweaving Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_VEILWEAVING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you shape your veils for the day, and whenever you reallocate your essence, you may select a number of creatures equal to or less than your casting ability modifier. These creatures take no damage from veils you have shaped, and if they must roll a saving throw against a veil you have shaped they are always treated as if they passed the saving throw when determining its effects. These creatures retain these benefits until you use this talent again. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/veilweaving#toc43
